      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This sounds like a fascinating challenge that blends intuition with rigorous data science. You might consider a hybrid model, perhaps using a Bayesian network to formally structure your intuitive \"spikes\" as latent variables influencing the probabilities of known stochastic events. You would need to quantify these spikes—perhaps mapping them to measurable features like unusual pattern recognition scores or cognitive load metrics—to embed them into the model. This allows you to treat your intuitive input not as a black box, but as a quantifiable prior belief that triggers a predictive adjustment in your likelihood functions.",
